; The alias-of-`any` fixture. CDDL `any` crosses the component face as the transparent `any-cbor`
; byte alias and comes back through `AnyCbor::from_cbor_bytes` at the consuming door, so every door
; that takes one must be FALLIBLE — the decode of arbitrary caller-supplied bytes IS the re-check.
; The projection's TYPE walk resolves a transparent CDDL alias at the use site, so the FALLIBILITY
; walk has to resolve it too: a walk that stops at the alias emits an infallible `constructor` over
; a body that decodes with `?`, which is perfectly valid WIT whose emitted glue does not compile
; (E0277). Nothing else in the committed corpus reaches `any` from a member position through an
; alias, which is why this fixture exists rather than a row on an existing one.

; A two-link alias CHAIN, so a walk that resolves exactly ONE link is caught here as well as one
; that resolves none.
shallow_any = any
deep_any = shallow_any

aliased = [
  ; Through the chain.
  chained: deep_any,
  ; Through a single link.
  single: shallow_any,
  ; The IN-FIXTURE CONTROL: the same `any`, written directly. Its door has always been fallible, so
  ; it is what the two aliased ones are compared against — an agreement failure in either direction
  ; is visible without leaving the fixture.
  direct: any,
]
